    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0117" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48/5115: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-23T14:00:00+01:00">September 23, 1941—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 23—10:06 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4471. Embassy’s 4458, September 22, 7 p.m.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d73-f1"/> The
                    Foreign Office informs me that the Allied meeting tomorrow morning will open in
                    private for organization purposes and then be opened to the public with
                    journalists present.</p>
                <p>There has been no substantive change in the draft resolution quoted in my No.
                    3615, August 23 [<hi rendition="#italic">13</hi>], 9 p.m., except in paragraph 6
                    which now provides that the bureau to be established by the British Government
                    will report to an Inter-Allied committee under the chairmanship of
                    Leith-Ross.</p>
                <p>The draft resolution will be proposed in a speech by Mr. Eden during the course
                    of which he will make the statement authorized on behalf of the United States.
                    Mr. Maisky<anchor n="26" xml:id="d73-f2"/> will deliver a statement of the
                    policy of the Russian Government. There will be a resolution by the Allied
                    Governments to adhere to the Atlantic Charter.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d73-f3"/>
                    The Polish and Czech representatives will separately state their views of the
                    application of the Charter to their countries but according to the Foreign <pb
                        facs="0118" n="110" xml:id="pg110"/> Office these are not in the nature of
                    reservations. The Polish and Czech representatives will also make a joint
                    statement of solidarity. Minutes of the meeting will be supplied to the
                    Embassy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[A report of the Inter-Allied Meeting of September 24, 1941, is printed as
                        British Cmd. 6315, Miscellaneous No. 3 (1941): <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Inter-Allied Meeting Held in London at St. James’s Palace on September
                            24, 1941, Report of Proceedings</hi>.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
